{"type":"message","id":"896cb8e6","parentId":"26bbc7ea","timestamp":"2026-05-24T20:07:19.727Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking \"how to verify\" - referring back to the previous message about external platforms where existing Coze/Feishu ports don't need verification unless recovering identity. They want to know what the verification process would look like when it IS needed (i.e., for new platforms or identity recovery scenarios).\n\nLet me think about this in the context of OpenClaw and the multi-channel setup. This seems to be about how to verify identity when connecting new external platforms or recovering identity.\n\nI should provide practical verification methods. Let me think about what makes sense:\n\n1. For new external platform connections - some form of identity verification\n2. For Feishu identity recovery - verification process\n\nLet me check if there's any existing protocol or documentation about this.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_944e90ec63ba456a88998006","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"身份核验 验证 外部平台 连接"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":415,"output":343,"cacheRead":32256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33014,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779653233035}}
