d every minute.\n66 Greed\nSTOCK MARKET FEAR & GREED\nS&P 500\n7,165.08+0.80%\nNASDAQ\n24,836.60+1.63%\nDow Jones\n492.31 -0.16%\n31 Fear\nCRYPTO MARKET FEAR & GREED\n▼ -8 pts\nBTC\n$77,539.77+0.11%\nETH\n$2,317.24+0.06%\nSOL\n$86.41+0.21%\nTrending Fear & Greed scores\nStocks Crypto\nName F&G Score Sentiment Price 24h % 5d % 1M %\nApple AAPL 55 Neutral $271.06 -0.87% +0.27% +7.30%\nNVIDIA NVDA 72 Greed $208.27 +4.32% +4.15% +16.56%\nMicrosoft MSFT 46 Neutral $424.62 +2.13% +0.82% +14.44%\nAmazon.com AMZN 68 Greed $263.99 +3.49% +5.94% +24.69%\nAlphabet GOOG 68 Greed $342.32 +1.35% +1.11% +18.21%\nMeta Platforms META 49 Neutral $675.03 +2.41% -0.93% +13.47%\nTesla TSLA 40 Fear $376.30 +0.69% -6.53% -2.50%\nBroadcom AVGO 79 Extreme Greed $422.76 +0.67% +4.21% +32.61%\nPalantir Technologies PLTR 38 Fear $143.09 +1.07% -1.32% -7.66%\nAdvanced Micro Devices AMD 90 Extreme Greed $347.81 +13.91% +23.95% +57.90%\nName F&G Score Sentiment Price 24h % 5d % 1M %\nBitcoin BTC 36 Fear $77,551.99 +0.12% +5.05% +8.77%\nEthereum ETH 39 Fear $2,316.19 +0.02% +2.31% +6.84%\nSolana SOL 26 Fear $86.34 +0.13% +3.40% -5.82%\nBNB BNB 34 Fear $637.33 +0.15% +3.40% -1.59%\nXRP XRP 28 Fear $1.43 -0.02% +2.77% +1.36%\nTron TRX 53 Neutral $0.32 +0.02% -1.61% +2.95%\nDogecoin DOGE 36 Fear $0.10 +0.32% +6.09% +2.70%\nHyperliquid HYPE 59 Greed $41.22 +0.08% +1.27% +2.28%\nCardano ADA 18 Extreme Fear $0.25 +0.34% +3.59% -7.03%\nChainlink LINK 29 Fear $9.41 +0.30% +3.76% +0.33%\nLatest market news & sentiment analysis\nStock\nChina's DeepRoute.ai says over 300,000 vehicles use its advanced driving system\nreuters.com · Apr 25, 2026\nCrypto\nBitcoin Mining Difficulty Set for 3% Friday Drop\naped.ai · Apr 25, 2026\nStock\nIran War Fallout Drives Inflation Risks in Africa | Bloomberg Next Africa\nyoutube.com · Apr 25, 2026\nCrypto\nSolana's next move may already be in motion – Big money is piling in!\nambcrypto.com · Apr 25, 2026\nUnderstanding the Fear & Greed Index - How it works\nWhat is the Fear & Greed Index?\nThe Fear & Greed Index measures investor sentiment on a scale of 0 to 100. Scores below 25 indicate Extreme Fear — often a signal of overselling and potential buying opportunities. Scores above 75 signal Extreme Greed — when markets may be overheated. Our proprietary scores combine RSI, ADX, SMA50, EMA200, Golden Cross signals, volatility, and social sentiment.\nHow to use sentiment for trading\nContrarian investors use the Fear & Greed Index to identify market extremes. When sentiment reaches Extreme Fear, markets have historically bounced. When it hits Extreme Greed, corrections often follow. Combine sentiment with technical and fundamental analysis for a data-driven edge in your stock picking or DCA strategy.\nStocks + Crypto sentiment in one place\nFear & Greed Tracker is the only platform that unifies stock and crypto sentiment analysis with AI-powered trading signals, trend predictions, and individual asset Fear & Greed scores for 50,000+ assets. Stop guessing — track the market's emotions in real time and make decisions backed by data.\n","publishTime":"2026-04-25T16:04:59+08:00"},{"title":"【天眼今日分析】马斯克再发推文 狗狗币涨超20%","url":"https://caifuhao.eastmoney.com/news/20210428180535050527280","siteName":"财富号","snippet":"其他灰度信托则为每日更新数据。\n贪婪指数\n今日比特币恐惧/贪婪指数59，昨日为50，\n指数阈值为0-100，其中值为0表示“极度恐惧”，而值为100则表示“极度贪婪”。包\n含指标：波动性（25%）＋市场交易量（25%）＋社媒热度（15%）＋市场调查（15%\n）＋比特币在整个市场中的比例（10%）＋谷歌热词分析（10%）。\n【要闻回顾】\n1、\n2、Visa首席执行官：Visa正大举进入加密货币领域。\n3、DeFi总锁仓量突破1","content":"【天眼今日分析】马斯克再发推文 狗狗币涨超20%\n中金网  2021年04月28日 18:05\n讯 : 【今日头条】\n欧盟投资银行首次利用区块链技术发行1亿欧元债券\n据知情人透露，欧洲投资银行计划为首次发行的利用区块链的两年期数字债券定价1亿欧元（1.21亿美元），该数字债券将在以太坊区块链上注册。这笔交易由高盛集团、桑坦德银行和法国 兴业银行管理。\n【盘面分析】\n从盘面上看，前十币种24小时涨幅榜涨跌不一，其中比特币维持横盘震荡之势徘徊于54000美元，以太坊盘中再创新高，史上首次突破2700美元大关。值得关注的是，由于特斯拉CEO埃隆马斯克（Elon Musk）再次发布有关DOGE的推文：The Dogefather，5月8号《周六夜现场》。狗狗币午后再度大涨，突破0.34美元关口，日内涨幅超20%。从日K图上看，比特币在48000美元附近企稳回升后，目前币价来到了前期的密集成交区域55000-60000美元附近，加上下方的量能有限，币价短期承压盘整。技术面上，下方的MACD指标显示做空继续放缓，但是目前仍处于空头市场，如果在55000美元稳固，后市有望进一步上探至6万美元大关。\n截至发稿，coingecko数据显示，主流币种24小时表现如下：\n图：主流币种24小时涨跌\n【数据分析】\n合约成交额\n截至发稿，当日全网期货市场成交额824.51亿美元。具体来看，OKEX成交96.69亿美元，huobi成交180.91亿美元，bybit成交78.18亿美元，binance成交403亿美元。\n图：期货市场成交量\n合约爆仓额\n24小时全网爆仓4.84亿美元，爆仓人数 91,103 人，最大单笔爆仓单发生在 Bitmex-ETH 价值 838.55万美元。\n从爆仓的详细数据看，多头爆仓金额2.87亿美元，空头爆仓1.96亿美元，多头爆仓占比59.41%。\n币种方面，日内再创历史新高并且首次站上2700美元大关的以太坊爆仓金额超越比特币登上首位，爆仓金额1.12亿美元，比特币爆仓金额1.08亿美元。消息面上，欧盟的投资与发展机构欧洲投资银行（EIB）开始对以太坊网络中注册的1亿欧元债券进行定价。\n此外，值得注意的是，MATIC爆仓金额排在比特币、以太坊、瑞波币、狗狗币之后位居第五位，行情数据显示，MATIC日内币价再创历史新高，以20%的涨幅继续强势领跑Layer2概念币版块。消息面上，以太坊推送服务（EPNS）宣布与以太坊扩容解决方案Polygon达成合作关系，将构建一个可以订阅 Polygon渠道和接受钱包通知的channel。通知内容可由用户自己定制，包括资金从Polygon L2成功转移到以太坊L1等。另外，合作内容还包括在EPNS协议中实施Polygon的基础架构，以提供可扩展的低成本通知服务；共同开发通知基础架构；为 MATIC 社区和Polygon项目开发通知服务以及共同开发以太坊生态系统的推送通知。\n图：24小时全网爆仓统计\n图：24小时各币种爆仓统计\n资金流向榜\n当日资金净流入MKR、DASH、ADA、WAVES、BCH等币种，其中MKR在昨日获得资金加仓首位后今天继续霸榜，获得资金加仓1.59亿美元。\n图：当日资金净流入前十\n而BTC、XRP、ETH、BNB、BTT等币种惨遭抛售，从资金流向看，比特币净流出金额高达9.94亿美元，此外瑞波币和以太坊分别净流出3.14亿美元和2.9亿美元分列第二、第三位。\n图：当日资金净流出前十\n主流币种多空\n24小时全网多空数据显示，比特币和以太坊的空头持仓均小幅占优，表明了市场对于比特币和以太坊的看空情绪提升，具体数据如下图：\n图：24小时全网交易所BTC多空比例\n图：24小时全网交易所ETH多空比例\n灰度动态\n截至美东时间4月27日，灰度总资产管理规模为455亿美元。灰度BTC、ETH、ETC、BCH、LTC信托当日未增持，GBTC溢价率-9.34%、ETHE溢价率2.47%、ETCG溢价率-3.27%、BCHG溢价率242.14%、LTCN溢价率898.24%。 灰度LINK信托持仓增持2996.68 LINK（+1.88%），灰度MANA信托持仓增持20709.43 MANA（+0.12%），灰度FIL信托持仓增持893.96 FIL（+1.81%）。具体来看，灰度信托持仓数据变化如下：\n图：灰度信托单资产基金信息\n注：灰度ZEC、XLM和ZEN三大信托官方每月更新持仓数据；其他灰度信托则为每日更新数据。\n贪婪指数\n今日比特币恐惧/贪婪指数59，昨日为50，贪婪程度有所上升，等级由“中性”转为“贪婪”。\n图：当日/历史比特币恐惧和贪婪指数\n注：恐慌指数阈值为0-100，其中值为0表示“极度恐惧”，而值为100则表示“极度贪婪”。包含指标：波动性（25%）＋市场交易量（25%）＋社媒热度（15%）＋市场调查（15%）＋比特币在整个市场中的比例（10%）＋谷歌热词分析（10%）。\n【要闻回顾】\n1、欧盟投资银行首次利用区块链技术发行1亿欧元债券。\n2、Visa首席执行官：Visa正大举进入加密货币领域。\n3、DeFi总锁仓量突破1000亿美元，创历史新高。\n4、ARK基金买入美团、京东、腾讯和Coinbase的股票。\n5、韩国游戏巨头Nexon已购买约1亿美元比特币。\n6、Ripple CEO：对于公司面对美SEC诉讼取得的进展“感觉良好”。\n【后市前瞻】\n币圈达人、行情分析师于集鑫认为，比特币早间的多头实力强劲，价格虽有回踩，但整体还是维持震荡上行的格局，操作建议回调多为主，可在关键压制位抓反弹空。DOT整体走势维持震荡上行的格局，操作建议回调多为主反弹空为辅。\n","publishTime":"2021-04-28T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"| AiCoin Real-time News","url":"https://www-tc.aicoin.com/en/news-flash/2881633","siteName":"AiCoin","snippet":" citing data from Alternative.me, today's cryptocurrency Fear and Gr\need Index has dropped to 42 (yesterday the index was 49, 'Neutral St\nate'), indicating that the market has shifted from 'Neutral State' t","content":"Foresight News | May 13, 2026 08:30\n[Today's Fear and Greed Index drops to 42, market shifts to 'Fear State'] According to Foresight News, citing data from Alternative.me, today's cryptocurrency Fear and Greed Index has dropped to 42 (yesterday the index was 49, 'Neutral State'), indicating that the market has shifted from 'Neutral State' to 'Fear State'.\n","publishTime":"2026-05-13T00:30:00+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779667371766}}
{"type":"message","id":"d24b9dff","parentId":"05d5bd38","timestamp":"2026-05-25T00:02:51.869Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3bf8da1a15f24732af8dcdd8","toolName":"coze_web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Coze web search: US stock market news today May 25 2026 pre market\n\nResults (5)\n1. 美股盘前交易\n   URL: https://cn.investing.com/equities/pre-market?chain_id=y_jvgw2cZD6mqO.1l0mumd&global_content=%7B%22promote_id%22%3A13766%2C%22sub_promote_id%22%3A14%2C%22f%22%3A%22www.futunn.com%2Flearn%2Fdetail-bottom-fishing-in-china-these-etf-are-worth-watching-91402-240906032%22%7D\n   Source: 英为财情Investing.com\n   Published: 2026-05-24T23:35:00+08:00\n   美股盘前交易\n美股盘前页面，免费提供美股盘前价格、盘前交易实时数据和最新新闻和消息。美国股票在最近盘前交易日以及该交易日中涨跌幅最大者的盘前行情与走势一览无余。 您可点击查看5种不同的股指或全美股市概览。\n链接到美国股市的最新新闻和分析。\n盘前\n盘前交易已结束\n盘前行情\nSPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average\n(DIA)\n507.44\n+4.33\n(+0.86%)\nInvesco\n2. US Stock and Hong Kong Stock Markets Closed on Monday, Early Close for Gold, Silver, and Oil Trading\n   URL: https://m.lookonchain.com/feeds/57507\n   Source: Lookonchain\n   Published: 2026-05-24T21:35:57+08:00\n   US Stock and Hong Kong Stock Markets Closed on Monday, Early Close f\nervance of Memorial Day, the U.S. stock market will remain fully clo\nsed on Monday, May 25. For CME Group futures contracts trading on Ma\n3. Stock Market Holiday Schedule: Memorial Day 2026\n   URL: https://ts2.tech/en/is-the-stock-market-open-on-memorial-day-2026-wall-streets-holiday-hours-before-a-big-week/\n   Source: TS2 Space\n   Published: 2026-05-22T10:56:00+08:00\n   t trades close to record highs as markets head into the long weekend\nMemorial Day brings a three-day pause for U.S. stock traders. Both t\nhe New York Stock Exchange and Nasdaq will shut on Monday, May 25, 2\n4. S&P 500 MARKET REACTION\n   URL: http://widgets.economictimes.com/topic/s&p-500-market-reaction/news\n   Source: The Economic Times\n   Published: 2026-05-23T09:12:00+08:00\n   arnings wind down, yields perk up\nUS stocks face potential headwinds\n as a strong earnings season concludes. Investors are shifting focus\nay, 2026, 09:12 AM IST\nU.S. stock market prediction for Thursday: S&\n5. Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026: Nifty at 23,719, Dow at Record 50,580 and US Markets Closed for Memorial Day\n   URL: https://univest.in/blogs/stock-market-predictions-for-tomorrow-25-may-2026\n   Source: Univest\n   Published: 2026-05-23T16:30:00+08:00\n   or tomorrow 25 May: Nifty 23,719. US Memorial Day holiday. Dow recor\n6 May monthly expiry Tuesday.\nThe stock market predictions for tomor\nrow on Monday 25 May 2026 are shaped by three features that make thi"}],"details":{"query":"US stock market news today May 25 2026 pre market","type":"web","count":5,"items":[{"title":"美股盘前交易","url":"https://cn.investing.com/equities/pre-market?chain_id=y_jvgw2cZD6mqO.1l0mumd&global_content=%7B%22promote_id%22%3A13766%2C%22sub_promote_id%22%3A14%2C%22f%22%3A%22www.futunn.com%2Flearn%2Fdetail-bottom-fishing-in-china-these-etf-are-worth-watching-91402-240906032%22%7D","siteName":"英为财情Investing.com","snippet":"美股盘前交易\n美股盘前页面，免费提供美股盘前价格、盘前交易实时数据和最新新闻和消息。美国股票在最近盘前交易日以及该交易日中涨跌幅最大者的盘前行情与走势一览无余。 您可点击查看5种不同的股指或全美股市概览。\n链接到美国股市的最新新闻和分析。\n盘前\n盘前交易已结束\n盘前行情\nSPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average\n(DIA)\n507.44\n+4.33\n(+0.86%)\nInvesco","content":"美股盘前交易\n美股盘前页面，免费提供美股盘前价格、盘前交易实时数据和最新新闻和消息。美国股票在最近盘前交易日以及该交易日中涨跌幅最大者的盘前行情与走势一览无余。 您可点击查看5种不同的股指或全美股市概览。 此页还提供美国财经日历链接以及财报季时的财报日历，并在页面底部可链接到美国股市的最新新闻和分析。\n盘前\n盘前交易已结束\n盘前行情\nSPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average\n(DIA)\n507.44\n+4.33\n(+0.86%)\nInvesco QQQ Trust\n(QQQ)\n717.71\n+3.20\n(+0.45%)\nSPDR标普500\n(SPY)\n746.48\n+3.76\n(+0.51%)\n罗素2000指数ETF-iShares\n(IWM)\n284.31\n+1.82\n(+0.64%)\n美股盘前最活跃股票\n名称\n代码\n最新\n涨跌额\n涨跌幅\n交易量\n看涨\n时间\n价格\nMicron MU 756.77 -5.33 -0.70% 1.54M\n+7.8%\n22/05 756.77 -5.33 -0.70%\nNVIDIA NVDA 221.05 +1.54 +0.70% 4.29M\n+7.8%\n22/05 221.05+1.54+0.70%\nAMD AMD 469.49 +19.90 +4.43% 1.5M\n+7.8%\n22/05 469.49+19.90+4.43%\nMicrosoft MSFT 419.38 +0.29 +0.07% 1.33M\n+7.8%\n22/05 419.38+0.29+0.07%\nIntel INTC 120.09 +1.59 +1.34% 3.78M\n+7.8%\n22/05 120.09+1.59+1.34%\nIBM IBM 261.64 +8.67 +3.43% 1.49M\n+7.8%\n22/05 261.64+8.67+3.43%\nTesla TSLA 422.50 +4.65 +1.11% 898.37K\n+7.8%\n22/05 422.50+4.65+1.11%\nAlphabet A GOOGL 387.25 -0.41 -0.11% 352.78K\n+7.8%\n22/05 387.25 -0.41 -0.11%\nQualcomm QCOM 214.00 +0.59 +0.28% 589.73K\n+7.8%\n22/05 214.00+0.59+0.28%\nServiceNow Inc NOW 102.02 +2.33 +2.34% 1.03M\n+7.8%\n22/05 102.02+2.33+2.34%\n美股盘前领涨股票\n名称\n价格\nEL\nEstee Lauder\n89.31 +10.40 +13.18%\nROST\nRoss Stores Inc\n231.60 +14.41 +6.63%\nTTWO\nTake-Two\n253.68 +15.60 +6.55%\nGNRC\nGenerac\n261.99 +14.20 +5.73%\nDELL\nDell Tech\n266.99 +14.19 +5.61%\nAME\nAmetek Inc\n234.81 +11.64 +5.22%\nAMD\nAMD\n469.49 +19.90 +4.43%\nBWA\nBorgWarner Inc\n66.29 +2.74 +4.31%\nMRK\nMerck&Co\n120.05 +4.17 +3.60%\nIBM\nIBM\n261.64 +8.67 +3.43%\n美股盘前领跌股票\n名称\n价格\nPPG\nPPG Industries Inc\n103.26 -3.37 -3.16%\nDVA\nDaVita\n192.86 -5.80 -2.92%\nEMN\nEastman Chemical\n71.33 -1.86 -2.54%\nCBOE\nCboe Global\n343.32 -8.62 -2.45%\nAJG\nArthur J Gallagher\n203.27 -4.14 -2.00%\nCBRE\nCBRE A\n128.77 -2.27 -1.73%\nLVS\nLas Vegas Sands\n48.60 -0.85 -1.72%\nWRB\nW. R. Berkley Corp\n66.35 -1.12 -1.66%\nWYNN\nWynn Resorts\n96.96 -1.58 -1.60%\nREGN\nRegeneron Pharma\n632.94 -9.65 -1.50%\n","publishTime":"2026-05-24T23:35:00+08:00"},{"title":"US Stock and Hong Kong Stock Markets Closed on Monday, Early Close for Gold, Silver, and Oil Trading","url":"https://m.lookonchain.com/feeds/57507","siteName":"Lookonchain","snippet":"US Stock and Hong Kong Stock Markets Closed on Monday, Early Close f\nervance of Memorial Day, the U.S. stock market will remain fully clo\nsed on Monday, May 25. For CME Group futures contracts trading on Ma","content":"US Stock and Hong Kong Stock Markets Closed on Monday, Early Close for Gold, Silver, and Oil Trading\n8 hours ago\n### Market Holiday & Early Trading Session Advisory **Effective May 25 Observations:** In observance of Memorial Day, the U.S. stock market will remain fully closed on Monday, May 25. For CME Group futures contracts trading on May 26 Beijing Time: - Precious metals and WTI crude oil futures will close early at 02:30 Beijing Time - U.S. stock index and Treasury futures will wrap up trading early at 01:00 Beijing Time In Asia-Pacific, Vesak Day holidays will impact markets on May 25: - The Hong Kong Stock Exchange is closed, with Southbound and Northbound trading links suspended - The South Korean stock market is also closed In Europe, the U.K. Spring Bank Holiday will lead to the closure of the U.K. stock market on May 25. ICE Brent crude oil futures will close early at 01:30 Beijing Time on May 26. Investors are urged to plan accordingly. Source: FXStreet\n","publishTime":"2026-05-24T21:35:57+08:00"},{"title":"Stock Market Holiday Schedule: Memorial Day 2026","url":"https://ts2.tech/en/is-the-stock-market-open-on-memorial-day-2026-wall-streets-holiday-hours-before-a-big-week/","siteName":"TS2 Space","snippet":"t trades close to record highs as markets head into the long weekend\nMemorial Day brings a three-day pause for U.S. stock traders. Both t\nhe New York Stock Exchange and Nasdaq will shut on Monday, May 25, 2","content":"22 May 2026\nStock Market\nStock Market Holiday Schedule: Memorial Day 2026\nby Marcin Frąckiewicz\nNEW YORK, May 22, 2026, 06:34 (EDT)\nU.S. stock markets will be closed Monday, May 25, for Memorial Day. That includes the NYSE and Nasdaq.\nThe bond market’s recommended close is set for 2 p.m. ET on Friday. Markets are closed Monday.\nWall Street trades close to record highs as markets head into the long weekend. Investors are looking to next week’s inflation data and AI-linked earnings.\nMemorial Day brings a three-day pause for U.S. stock traders. Both the New York Stock Exchange and Nasdaq will shut on Monday, May 25, 2026. Stock trading stops for the federal holiday. The Office of Personnel Management lists Memorial Day as Monday, May 25, and both the NYSE and Nasdaq show that day as closed on their holiday schedules.\nThe issue is on traders’ minds now as the shutdown hits when Wall Street is looking to hang on to May’s rally despite new worries over inflation, oil, and Treasury yields. Regular NYSE trading hours are 9:30 a.m. to 4 p.m. ET, the same for Nasdaq’s main market, so the next scheduled session after the holiday is Tuesday unless exchanges announce otherwise.\nBond traders will see an early close before the weekend. SIFMA, the Wall Street group that sets the fixed-income calendar, suggests a 2 p.m. ET close on Friday, May 22, ahead of the Memorial Day break. The shortened session applies to debt markets like Treasuries and corporates.\nFutures for major U.S. stock indexes traded higher early Friday, Reuters said, with Treasury yields dropping and big tech shares ticking up. As of 4:55 a.m. ET, Dow futures were up 0.3%. Futures for the S&P 500 rose 0.31%, and Nasdaq 100 futures gained 0.5%.\nS&P 500 climbed 0.2% to 7,445.72 on Thursday as stocks ticked up. The Dow Jones Industrial Average advanced 0.6% to 50,285.66. Nasdaq Composite was up 0.1% at 26,293.10. Moves came as Brent crude gave up earlier gains, falling back under $103 after trading above $109.\nHoliday or not, pressure remains. Naeem Aslam, chief investment officer at Zaye Capital Markets, told Reuters, “geopolitical risk has become less immediately damaging for sentiment,” but said investors are still following U.S.-Iran talks, the Strait of Hormuz, and oil-supply risk. Reuters\nMarkets face a busy run of data in a shortened week. Reuters said investors have their eyes on Thursday’s personal consumption expenditures price index, or PCE, which is the Fed’s main inflation measure. Also on tap: a new look at first-quarter GDP and the latest read on consumer confidence. “The macro environment is starting to take more center stage,” said Anthony Saglimbene, chief market strategist at Ameriprise. Reuters\nEarnings season isn’t quite over. Nvidia projected second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, topping forecasts, as its chips stay at the heart of AI spending. Investors will get numbers from Salesforce and Dell—both tied to AI—next week. Brock Weimer, investment strategy analyst at Edward Jones, said Nvidia’s results show “robust AI-related spending trends remain intact.” Reuters\nUBS Global Wealth Management bumped its 2026 year-end S&P 500 target to 7,900 from 7,500 on Friday, pointing to steady consumer spending and data-center demand. The new forecast calls for around 6% upside from the index’s last close. UBS also raised its 2026 earnings-per-share estimate to $335 from $310.\nRisks are looking more immediate. Treasury yields have jumped as markets grow nervous that rising oil prices and supply troubles could keep inflation up. Higher yields tend to hurt stocks by making debt more expensive and drawing some money away from equities. “Inflation concerns continue to flare,” Jim Baird, chief investment officer at Plante Moran Financial Advisors, told Reuters. Reuters\nTraders get a break from regular U.S. stock trading on Memorial Day 2026. Markets come back Tuesday with the S&P near highs, facing new inflation numbers, yield moves, and another shot at the AI trade.\n","publishTime":"2026-05-22T10:56:00+08:00"},{"title":"S&P 500 MARKET REACTION","url":"http://widgets.economictimes.com/topic/s&p-500-market-reaction/news","siteName":"The Economic Times","snippet":"arnings wind down, yields perk up\nUS stocks face potential headwinds\n as a strong earnings season concludes. Investors are shifting focus\nay, 2026, 09:12 AM IST\nU.S. stock market prediction for Thursday: S&","content":"SEARCHED FOR:\nS&P 500 MARKET REACTION\nWall Street Week Ahead: Soaring stocks could face rocky patch as earnings wind down, yields perk up\nUS stocks face potential headwinds as a strong earnings season concludes. Investors are shifting focus to rising inflation and bond yields, with the PCE price index due Thursday. Futures now price in a potential Fed rate hike later in 2026, a stark contrast to earlier expectations. Key reports from Salesforce and Costco are awaited.\n23 May, 2026, 09:12 AM IST\nU.S. stock market prediction for Thursday: S&P 500, Dow Jones, Nasdaq, Russell 2000 eye positive trading\nU.S. stock market bounced back after pressure eased on Wall Street from the bond market and oil prices gave back some of their big gains.\n21 May, 2026, 06:52 AM IST\nUS stocks today: S&P 500, Nasdaq open higher as chip stocks gain ahead of Nvidia results\nUS markets opened mixed with the S&P 500 and Nasdaq gaining on a rebound in chip stocks ahead of Nvidia’s earnings, seen as a key gauge of AI demand. The Dow slipped slightly as investors remained cautious about elevated Treasury yields and their impact on valuations.\n20 May, 2026, 07:08 PM IST\nUS stock market on Wednesday: S&P 500, Dow Jones, Nasdaq to fall again today? These factors offer hints\nUS Stock Market today: Dow Jones, S&P 500, Nasdaq investors are looking for positive turnaround in the Wall Street.\n20 May, 2026, 07:25 AM IST\nUS stock market crashes today: Dow Jones, S&P 500, and Nasdaq fall hard as bond yields hit 19-year high - Nvidia, Broadcom, AMD, and Amazon lead massive Wall Street selloff\nUS stock market crashes today as Dow Jones, S&P 500 and Nasdaq plunge. The Dow Jones Industrial Average dropped more than 237 points, while the S&P 500 and Nasdaq slid deeper into negative territory as technology and AI-linked stocks faced heavy selling pressure. A perfect storm of soaring Treasury yields, oil above $100, and a violent unwind in semiconductor stocks sent Wall Street into its third straight day of losses.\n19 May, 2026, 09:30 PM IST\nUS stocks today: S&P 500 and Nasdaq open lower as chip stocks drag, inflation fears persist\nThe S&P 500 and the Nasdaq opened lower on Tuesday, pressured by a ⁠selloff ⁠in heavyweight chip stocks and lingering inflation concerns as Treasury yields continued to rise.\n19 May, 2026, 07:07 PM IST\nUS stocks today: S&P 500, Nasdaq open higher as chips rebound, yields retreat\nThe S&P 500 and the Nasdaq opened higher on Monday as heavyweight semiconductor ⁠stocks ⁠recovered, while a bond market rout that had sparked a selloff the previous week ⁠appeared to cool.\nBond yield spike puts equities market at risk\nInvestors warn that US stock markets are not reflecting inflation risks. High energy prices and the Iran conflict are overlooked. A recent spike in bond yields is causing caution. Experts note a market paradox with strong earnings but negative inflation signals. Clients are seeking clarity on this divided outlook. This situation could impact company profits and economic growth.\nWhy is US stock market falling today? Dow Jones, S&P 500 and Nasdaq crash after Trump concludes China visit - Nvidia and Amazon stocks sink amid inflation fears and Iran war uncertainty shaking Wall Street\nUS stock market today suffered a sharp selloff as the Dow Jones, S&P 500, and Nasdaq crashed after President Donald Trump ended his China visit without easing deeper market fears. The S&P 500 fell 0.86% to 7,436, the Nasdaq dropped 1.25%, and the Dow lost 366 points to 49,697. Nvidia stock dropped nearly 4%. Amazon shares also slipped as rising Treasury yields, stubborn US inflation, and growing Iran war uncertainty shook Wall Street confidence. Oil climbed above $108. The dollar strengthened. Gold and silver plunged.\nUS Stock Market on Friday: S&P 500, Dow Jones, Nasdaq to crash today or these factors will uplift Wall Street? details here\nUS Stock Market today: Nasdaq, S&P 500, and Dow Jones investors will hope that Wall Street indexes will end the week in a strong note.\nUS stock market jumps sharply today as Dow Jones reclaims 50,000 — Why the Dow, S&P 500 and Nasdaq are all in green after U.S.-China trade summit boost\nUS stock market jumps sharply today as the Dow Jones, S&P 500 and Nasdaq rally on renewed optimism from the U.S.-China trade summit and booming AI demand. Nvidia and Cisco led Wall Street gains while investors balanced strong earnings against inflation fears and rising oil prices. The Dow Jones Industrial Average climbed more than 260 points while the S&P 500 and Nasdaq hit fresh highs behind strong technology gains and growing AI optimism.\nU.S. Stock Market on Wednesday: Dow Jones, S&P 500, Nasdaq to bounce back or Wall Street crash is happening? Check important factors\nU.S. Stock Market: U.S. dollar advanced for a second straight session after the economic data and amid uncertainty over the durability of the U.S.-Iran ceasefire.\nS&P 500, Nasdaq futures rise to new highs as Nvidia jumps\nNvidia rose 1.9% in premarket trading, giving the chipmaker a market valuation of $5.9 trillion, ⁠after ⁠Reuters reported citing sources that the U.S. has cleared about 10 Chinese firms to buy its second-most powerful AI chip, the H200\nFrom joke to 50X jackpot: American billionaire's simple ‘India-born CEO’ stock-picking idea would have made you a millionaire in 15 years\nA old joke by financier Michael Milken about investing in US companies led by Indian-born CEOs has sparked renewed interest. New analysis suggests this strategy could have delivered exceptional returns, significantly outperforming the S&P 500 over the past 15 years. This highlights the growing influence of Indian-origin leaders in American corporations, particularly in the tech sector.\nWhy did the US stock market crash today? Dow Jones, S&P 500 and Nasdaq sink deep into red as Iran tensions and soaring oil prices fuel fresh inflation fears across Wall Street\nUS stock market crash today shocked Wall Street after US CPI inflation jumped to 3.8%, the highest level in three years. The Dow Jones fell more than 307 points to 49,396.89, while the S&P 500 declined 0.63% to 7,366.24. The Nasdaq Composite dropped nearly 1%. Tech stocks lost momentum. Nvidia, Amazon, and Microsoft slipped as fears of longer Federal Reserve interest rates returned.\nU.S Stock Market today: S&P 500 stocks show signs of historic Wall Street crash, bear market but expert notes ray of hope\nU.S. Stock Market index S&P 500 is predicted to extend its rally in 2026, even as Middle East tensions disrupt ⁠global ⁠energy flows and drive inflation higher.\nU.S Stock Market on Tuesday: S&P 500, Dow Jones, Nasdaq for record trading? These factors will decide\nU.S. Stock market investors would hope that S&P 500, Dow Jones, Nasdaq will continue record run.\nWall Street upside? HSBC sees S&P 500 at 8,000, raises 2026 target as AI boom and tech earnings fuel optimism\nHSBC raised its 2026 S&P 500 target to 7,650, citing strong corporate earnings and resilient technology stocks. The brokerage said improving AI adoption, broader market participation and easing macro conditions could potentially push the index beyond the 8,000 mark despite lingering inflation and oil price risks.\nWhy are Dow Jones and S&P 500 down and Nasdaq up today, and will US stock market futures stay in red or turn green again? Full market explainer\nWhy are Dow Jones and S&P 500 down and Nasdaq up today, and will US stock market futures stay in red or turn green again? US stock market futures showed mixed movement as oil prices rose after stalled US-Iran talks. Investors reacted to inflation data expectations, corporate earnings, and geopolitical risks. Technology stocks supported Nasdaq gains while airline and gold mining stocks slipped. Markets now wait for inflation data, economic reports, and global meetings to decide the next direction.\n","publishTime":"2026-05-23T09:12:00+08:00"},{"title":"Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026: Nifty at 23,719, Dow at Record 50,580 and US Markets Closed for Memorial Day","url":"https://univest.in/blogs/stock-market-predictions-for-tomorrow-25-may-2026","siteName":"Univest","snippet":"or tomorrow 25 May: Nifty 23,719. US Memorial Day holiday. Dow recor\n6 May monthly expiry Tuesday.\nThe stock market predictions for tomor\nrow on Monday 25 May 2026 are shaped by three features that make thi","content":"Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026: Nifty at 23,719, Dow at Record 50,580 and US Markets Closed for Memorial Day\n23 May 2026 •\n5:41 pm\nPosted by: Ankit Jaiswal\nStock market predictions for tomorrow 25 May: Nifty 23,719. US Memorial Day holiday. Dow record 50,580. 26 May monthly expiry Tuesday.\nThe stock market predictions for tomorrow on Monday 25 May 2026 are shaped by three features that make this a structurally unique session in the May 2026 trading calendar. The Nifty 50 closed at 23,719.30 and the Sensex settled at 75,415.35 on Friday 22 May, with bank stocks and financial services leading the rally while the Rupee strengthened 51 paise to 95.69 against the Dollar on RBI intervention. US markets are closed on Monday 25 May for the Memorial Day holiday, removing the overnight directional cue that Indian traders rely on for opening positioning. And Tuesday 26 May is the Nifty 50 and Bank Nifty monthly options expiry day, making Monday the critical pre-expiry positioning session.\nAnkit Jaiswal, Senior Research Analyst at Univest, notes that the stock market predictions for tomorrow on Monday are the most technically complex of the month. With no US overnight guidance, Monday’s direction will be set entirely by Asian markets opening at 7:00 AM IST, European futures and the Iran-US peace deal trajectory over the weekend. Kunal Singla, Associate Director at Univest, adds that this market prediction for tomorrow prediction is constructively positive on the Dow Jones setting a fresh record at 50,580 (+294 pts, +0.58%) and the S&P 500 logging its eighth consecutive weekly gain, the longest winning streak since December 2023.\nTable of Contents\nFriday 22 May 2026 Market Recap for Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow\nAnalyst Watchlist: Stocks to Watch on Monday 25 May 2026\nNifty 50 Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow Monday 25 May 2026\nGlobal Cues for Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026\nSector Outlook for Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow\nPrivate Banks and Financial Services: Positive\nPharma: Post-Results Stabilisation Watch\nEnergy and OMCs: Iran Deal is the Binary\nIT: Neutral, Awaiting Fresh Catalyst\nKey Risks to Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow\nStock Market Predictions for Tomorrow: Quick Reference\nConclusion: Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026\nFAQs\nWhat are the stock market predictions for tomorrow on Monday 25 May 2026?\nWhy are US markets closed on Monday 25 May 2026?\nWhich are the top stocks to watch in the tomorrow market prediction for 25 May 2026?\nWhat is the significance of the 26 May 2026 Nifty monthly expiry for Monday?\nHow does the US-Iran peace deal affect stock market predictions for tomorrow?\nFriday 22 May 2026 Market Recap for Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow\nNifty 50 and Sensex: Nifty ended at 23,719.30 (+0.27%) and Sensex at 75,415.35 (+0.31%) in a session driven by private bank outperformance and RBI-driven Rupee recovery. Nifty attempted to cross its 20-day EMA but faced resistance and closed just below it, a technical level that features centrally in the nifty prediction for tomorrow on Monday.\nBank Nifty Surges 1.15 Per Cent: Bank Nifty rose 616 points or 1.15 per cent to close at 54,055, with intraday high of 54,213.05. Axis Bank gained 2.52 per cent to Rs 1,278, ICICI Bank rose 1.91 per cent to Rs 1,268, and Kotak Mahindra Bank advanced 1.06 per cent. Trent was the top Sensex gainer at Rs 4,295.75 (+3.01%). This private bank and financial services leadership is the central positive in the tomorrow market prediction.\nFII Net Sold Rs 4,440 Crore Despite Market Gains: FIIs net sold Rs 4,440.47 crore on 22 May even as the market closed higher. DIIs absorbed this with their largest single-day net buying of the week at Rs 6,003.53 crore. This DII-FII divergence of Rs 10,444 crore is the most important institutional flow data point for the stock market predictions for tomorrow on Monday.\nRupee Strengthens on RBI Intervention: The Reserve Bank of India intervened in forex markets to arrest Rupee weakness, driving the currency to an intraday high of 95.69 against the US Dollar, a strengthening of 51 paise from the previous close of 96.20. A stronger Rupee reduces FII hedging costs in Indian equities and is a positive structural signal for the tomorrow share market prediction.\nSun Pharma Falls 2.68 Per Cent Post Results: Sun Pharma fell to Rs 1,840.45 despite Q4 FY26 PAT growth of 26 per cent to Rs 2,714 crore and a final dividend of Rs 5 per share (total FY26 dividend Rs 16 per share). The sell-off was driven by EBITDA margin compression from 28.7 per cent to 27.1 per cent, dragging the Nifty Pharma and Healthcare indices lower on the day.\nNifty Media Worst Performer, Down 1.4 Per Cent: The Nifty Media index fell 1.4 per cent, the weakest sectoral performer on 22 May, reflecting continued pressure on advertising-dependent businesses amid the uncertain macro environment.\nAnalyst Watchlist: Stocks to Watch on Monday 25 May 2026\nAnkit Jaiswal and Kunal Singla have identified five stocks to monitor on Monday 25 May, based on 22 May closing prices and confirmed catalysts. These are analysis levels in the stock market predictions for tomorrow and do not constitute buy or sell recommendations.\nStock CMP (22 May close) Watch Level for Monday Catalyst Analyst Bias\nAxis Bank Rs 1,278 Above Rs 1,285 Top Sensex gainer (+2.52%) on 22 May; private bank leadership; RBI Rupee support; pre-monthly expiry bank buying Positive; sector momentum\nICICI Bank Rs 1,268 Above Rs 1,275 Nifty Private Bank outperformed 22 May; DII net buying Rs 6,003 Cr; consistent institutional support Positive; DII-backed\nTrent Rs 4,296 Above Rs 4,310 Top Sensex gainer +3.01% on 22 May; strong earnings momentum; Dow at record 50,580; consumer recovery Positive; strong momentum\nSun Pharma Rs 1,840 Above Rs 1,860 Post-Q4 dip recovery play; Q4 PAT +26% YoY; final dividend Rs 5/share; total FY26 dividend Rs 16 Recovery play; results absorbed\nIOC Rs 138 Above Rs 139 Crude at $105.56 easing; US-Iran deal progress could push crude lower; OMC margin expansion Mildly positive; Iran catalyst\nAxis Bank and ICICI Bank are the two highest-conviction picks in the stock market predictions for tomorrow watchlist because the private bank outperformance on 22 May was backed by the largest DII single-day net buying of the week at Rs 6,003.53 crore and RBI Rupee support that reduces FII hedging costs in financial stocks. Trent’s 3.01 per cent gain to Rs 4,296 reflects strong earnings momentum and the Dow Jones at a fresh record of 50,580, which extends the consumer discretionary recovery in the tomorrow nifty prediction for Monday. Sun Pharma at Rs 1,840 is the recovery play: Q4 PAT growth of 26 per cent and a total FY26 dividend of Rs 16 per share are fundamentally strong, and the post-results sell-off on EBITDA margin compression may be an overshoot in the tomorrow share market prediction. IOC at Rs 138 is the Iran peace deal beneficiary: a confirmed deal over the weekend would push crude below $105.56 and sharply expand OMC refining margins.\nNifty 50 Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow Monday 25 May 2026\nNifty Close (22 May): 23,719.30 (+0.27%)\nSensex Close (22 May): 75,415.35 (+0.31%)\nBank Nifty Close: 54,055 (+1.15%)\nNifty May Futures (early Saturday signal): 23,720 (-45 pts, -0.19%)\n20-Day EMA (Nifty Bull Pivot): Near 23,750\nKey Support: 23,550 and 23,450\nKey Resistance: 23,938 and 24,000\n26 May Monthly Expiry: Tuesday, 1 session away\nJaiswal’s tomorrow nifty 50 prediction for 25 May is cautiously positive to range-bound between 23,550 support and 23,938 resistance. The early Saturday Nifty May futures at 23,720 minus 45 points suggests a cautious open near 23,670 to 23,690 for Monday. However, the absence of US market cues (Memorial Day) means the first 15-minute candle after the 9:15 AM IST open will entirely determine Monday’s direction in the stock market predictions for tomorrow.\nSingla’s nifty tomorrow prediction focuses on the 20-day EMA near 23,750 that capped Nifty’s upside on 22 May. A sustained 15-minute close above 23,750 on Monday would confirm the 20-day EMA breakout and shift the tomorrow nifty prediction bullish toward 23,938, the confirmed technical breakout level. The 26 May monthly expiry on Tuesday means Monday has maximum pre-expiry institutional positioning activity, amplifying any directional move.\nGlobal Cues for Stock Market Predictions for Tomorrow 25 May 2026\nUS Markets Closed (Memorial Day): US markets are closed on Monday 25 May 2026 for the Memorial Day national holiday. With no Nasdaq, S&P 500 or Dow Jones overnight readings, Indian traders will rely entirely on Asian markets and European futures on Monday morning. The last US reading is Friday’s Dow at a fresh record of 50,580 (+0.58%), S&P 500 at its eighth consecutive weekly gain and Nasdaq +0.2 per cent. This is the dominant structural feature of the stock market predictions for tomorrow on Monday.\nUS-Iran Peace Deal Draft Reportedly Near: Reports on 22 May suggested a final draft resolution in the US-Iran conflict was expected imminently, pushing all four US indices higher and briefly pushing WTI below $100 per barrel. If a confirmed deal arrives over the weekend, Monday’s stock market predictions for tomorrow turn powerfully bullish: crude falls further, Rupee strengthens, and banks, infrastructure and OMC stocks rally sharply. A breakdown in talks reverses Friday’s optimism entirely.\nDow Jones at Fresh Record 50,580: The Dow Jones hit an intraday record on 22 May, closing at 50,580 (+294 pts). The S&P 500 logged its eighth consecutive weekly gain, the longest winning streak since December 2023. This sustained US equity strength is the most positive medium-term global signal in the stock market predictions for tomorrow for Indian markets.\nSpaceX IPO Filing Confirmed for June 12: SpaceX confirmed a regulatory filing for an IPO targeting June 12 at a valuation of 1.75 trillion US Dollars on the Nasdaq, potential...","publishTime":"2026-05-23T16:30:00+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779667371867}}
