{"type":"message","id":"9503e70b","parentId":"76a1bcdd","timestamp":"2026-05-25T13:51:02.308Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN is asking how I normally access hermes-sync to modify files. Good question - let me check if there's a token stored somewhere for hermes-sync, or if the hermes-skills repo's token could work for both.\n\nLooking at the URLs:\n- hermes-skills: `https://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-skills.git`\n- hermes-sync: `https://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync.git`\n\nWait, the hermes-sync URL also has `xianfanhuang:@github.com` - the `@` after the colon suggests there was a token there. Let me check if the token might be in a different location or if the clone lost it.\n\n\nThe clone succeeded with authentication, but the push is failing - that's odd. Let me look at what git credential helpers might be configured and whether the remote URL got altered during the clone process.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b1f68226c3514c71ac5715af","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check hermes-skills repo's remote URL for token\ncd /workspace/projects && git remote get-url origin\necho \"---\"\n# Check hermes-sync cloned URL\ncd /tmp/hermes-sync && git remote get-url origin\necho \"---\"\n# Check if there's a .git-credentials or credential helper\ncat ~/.git-credentials 2>/dev/null || echo \"no .git-credentials\"\ngit config --global --list 2>/dev/null | grep -i credential"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":521,"output":519,"cacheRead":77952,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":78992,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779717050836}}
{"type":"message","id":"38e5c079","parentId":"9503e70b","timestamp":"2026-05-25T13:51:02.321Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b1f68226c3514c71ac5715af","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"https://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-skills.git\n---\nhttps://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync.git\n---\nno .git-credentials\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":1,"durationMs":8,"aggregated":"https://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-skills.git\n---\nhttps://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync.git\n---\nno .git-credentials\n\n(Command exited with code 1)","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779717062319}}
{"type":"message","id":"8a91a023","parentId":"38e5c079","timestamp":"2026-05-25T13:51:19.124Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - both repos have the same URL pattern `xianfanhuang:@github.com` (the `@` after colon with nothing between means no token/password). But hermes-skills works for push while hermes-sync doesn't.\n\nWait, the `:` before `@` might mean there's a credential helper or the token is stored somewhere else. Let me check if the OpenClaw environment has a GitHub token set up differently.\n\nActually, looking more carefully - the URL `xianfanhuang:@github.com` means the password field is empty. Maybe there's a credential manager or the token is in environment variables. Let me check more thoroughly.\n\nAlso, I should check if maybe the hermes-skills repo was set up with a token that was later removed from the URL, and it's using cached credentials.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e5ed4028c94f42fd887ebe86","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's a GitHub token in OpenClaw config\ncat /workspace/projects/.openclaw/workspace-state.json 2>/dev/null\necho \"---\"\n# Check environment for any token\nenv | grep -i token 2>/dev/null | head -5\necho \"---\"\n# Try to find git credentials stored anywhere\nfind / -name \".git-credentials\" -o -name \"git-credential*\" 2>/dev/null | head -5\necho \"---\"\n# Check if credential store has anything\ngit credential-store 2>/dev/null\necho \"---\"\n# Check netrc\ncat ~/.netrc 2>/dev/null || echo \"no netrc\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":396,"output":499,"cacheRead":78464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79359,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779717062323}}
