{"type":"message","id":"f52d8dad","parentId":"2cd489f0","timestamp":"2026-05-25T13:51:52.041Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both repos have the same URL pattern with no token. But hermes-skills works for push while hermes-sync doesn't. This is strange. \n\nWait - maybe the hermes-skills push works because there's a cached credential from when the repo was originally cloned (perhaps with a token that was later removed from the URL). Or maybe there's a credential helper that I'm not seeing.\n\nActually, the most likely explanation is that the hermes-skills repo was originally cloned with a token embedded in the URL, and the git credential cache still has it. But hermes-sync was cloned without that cached credential.\n\nOr maybe... let me try to actually push to hermes-skills to verify it works, and then try a different approach for hermes-sync.\n\n\nLet me check if I can push to hermes-sync by first verifying whether hermes-skills can actually push, then testing with a GitHub token from a different source.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b8c1d938b7b9479b931c8417","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Test: can hermes-skills actually push?\ncd /workspace/projects && git push --dry-run origin main 2>&1 | head -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":381,"output":430,"cacheRead":79488,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80299,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779717101397}}
