{"type":"message","id":"4c07f816","parentId":"3ee6532d","timestamp":"2026-05-25T14:03:59.455Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API isn't working. Let me try a completely different approach - maybe I can create the askpass script myself using the Coze workload identity API. The script typically needs to output credentials when git asks for them.\n\nActually, let me look at this from a different angle. Maybe there's a simpler way - let me check if there's a way to use the Coze workload identity token directly for GitHub authentication. Or maybe I should just tell VAN that the askpass script is missing and we need to recreate it.\n\nActually, let me try to look at what the script should look like based on the Coze platform documentation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f399a61ed7c642d0a14068fe","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try to get a GitHub token using the workload identity\n# The Coze platform might provide this through a specific endpoint\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 10 \\\n  \"https://integration.coze.cn/api/v3/ai/agent_run/git_credential\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${COZE_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET}\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\necho \"---\"\n# Try the Coze coding endpoint\ncurl -s --connect-timeout 10 \\\n  \"https://api.coze.cn/.well-known/token\" \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"client_id\\\":\\\"${COZE_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID}\\\",\\\"client_secret\\\":\\\"${COZE_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET}\\\",\\\"grant_type\\\":\\\"client_credentials\\\"}\" 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\ntry:\n    d=json.load(sys.stdin)\n    for k,v in d.items():\n        if isinstance(v, str) and len(v)>50:\n            print(f'{k}: {v[:20]}...')\n        else:\n            print(f'{k}: {v}')\nexcept Exception as e: print(f'error: {e}')\n\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"API unavailable\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiao