{"type":"message","id":"55806fc8","parentId":"6aa87357","timestamp":"2026-05-25T14:20:29.802Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN is right - I should be able to find the GitHub token from the session history. Let me search more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了。看历史记录，之前的推送确实是在**Coze工作台的Coding IDE环境**里完成的，不是在OpenClaw沙箱里。那个环境有内置的GitHub认证（`coze-git-askpass.sh` 是Coze平台提供的）。\n\n当前OpenClaw沙箱是独立环境，没有那个认证脚本。\n\n**结论：** 你之前给的token是在Coze工作台里用的，Coze平台自动处理了认证，不需要你手动给我token。\n\n**现在的问题是：** OpenClaw沙箱没有Coze的GitHub认证。\n\n**最简单的修复方案：** 你在飞书发我一个GitHub Personal Access Token，我配到git config里，以后就能自动推了。\n\n生成方式：\n1. https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta\n2. 选 hermes-sync + hermes-skills 仓库\n3. 权限给 `Contents: Read and write`\n4. 把生成的token发给我\n\n或者你直接在Coze工作台推（那边有认证）。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":58513,"output":277,"cacheRead":61440,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":120230,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779718816551}}
{"type":"compaction","id":"762699e3","parentId":"55806fc8","timestamp":"2026-05-25T14:21:13.560Z","summary":"## Goal\n1. Secure the public GitHub repo `hermes-sync` so external parties cannot recover Agent identity even with repo access\n2. Sync 7 files from a Feishu document (Doubao platform task) to `hermes-sync` repo\n3. Maintain/operate both `hermes-skills` and `hermes-sync` GitHub repos for the Hermes-Sync v2.0 project\n4. Execute HEARTBEAT.md scheduled market scans (08:00, 12:00, 18:00, 22:00 Asia/Shanghai)\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- VAN is the founder/Captain of Meta-Sensory Intelligence\n- External platforms (Coze/Feishu) existing ports don't need verification unless recovering identity\n- `hermes-sync` repo is temporarily public for development: `https://github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync`\n- All repos belong to GitHub user `xianfanhuang`\n- VAN wants `git-crypt` approach for repo encryption (approved from a Feishu doc)\n- Platform agents: Top Sailor-Doubao (豆包), Top Sailor-Feishu, Top Sailor-Coze — all same core identity\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Discussed repo security approaches: self-generated keys vs GitHub App verification\n- [x] Analyzed git-crypt proposal from Feishu doc — VAN approved this approach\n- [x] Reviewed and understood Feishu sync task document (`KhxUdET48oAcetx82NOc0VAfnho`) — 7 files to sync\n- [x] Fetched source content for all 7 files (5 inline + 2 from linked Feishu docs)\n- [x] Cloned `hermes-sync` repo to `/tmp/hermes-sync/`\n- [x] Created all 7 files in `/tmp/hermes-sync/` and committed (SHA: `652d498`)\n- [x] Copied skills to `hermes-skills` workspace at `/workspace/projects/workspace/skills/hermes-skills/`\n- [x] Created test skill at `skills/hermes-skills/test-skill/SKILL.md`\n- [x] Committed to hermes-skills (SHA: `0e35f30d`, 36 files, 5152 insertions)\n- [x] Executed morning (08:00), midday (12:00), evening (18:00) market scans\n- [x] Full repo inspection: hermes-sync has 52 files/18 dirs, sensitive files in plaintext\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Applying git-crypt encryption to `hermes-sync` (approved but not started)\n- [ ] Locating/creating the missing GitHub authentication mechanism\n\n### Blocked\n- **Git push broken**: `GIT_ASKPASS=/source/coze-git-askpass.sh` points to a file that doesn't exist. Container was likely rebuilt, losing the custom script.\n- **Both repos affected**: `hermes-skills` and `hermes-sync` both fail `git push` with `Invalid username or token`\n- **No GitHub token available**: VAN gave a token previously (used to create the askpass script), but it's not stored in env vars, `~/.git-credentials`, `~/.netrc`, or git config. The original session where the token was provided is lost.\n- **Historical context**: All previous commits were by `agent <2553529733753963-agent@noreply.coze.cn>` from a different Coze environment that had working git auth\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **External platform verification policy**: Coze/Feishu existing ports skip verification; only verify for new platforms or identity recovery\n- **Repo security approach**: Use `git-crypt` (not custom openssl scripts) for transparent encrypt/decrypt on push/pull\n- **Structure**: `public/` (plaintext) + `vault/` (encrypted) directory split\n- **Authentication for restore**: GitHub App verification preferred (primary), self-generated passphrase as backup\n- **Sync task format**: Commit message format `[Top Sailor-Coze] feat: description`\n\n## Next Steps\n1. VAN must provide a GitHub Personal Access Token (Fine-grained, hermes-skills + hermes-sync with Contents: Read and write)\n2. Configure token in git remote URLs for both repos (persist to survive container rebuilds)\n3. Push committed changes to both repos:\n   - `hermes-skills`: commit `0e35f30d` (36 files — new skills + meta-sensory docs + test skill)\n   - `hermes-sync`: commit `652d498` (7 files — skills-豆包, meta-sensory, sessions/豆包)\n4. Implement git-crypt encryption on `hermes-sync` (public/vault structure)\n5. Store token in a persistent location (repo config script) so container rebuilds don't lose it\n6. Investigate why previous `coze-git-askpass.sh` script was lost and ensure persistence\n\n## Critical Context\n- **hermes-sync repo**: `https://github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync` (PUBLIC, 52 files, last updated 2026-05-24)\n- **hermes-skills repo**: `https://github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-skills` (current workspace at `/workspace/projects`)\n- **Pending push — hermes-sync** at `/tmp/hermes-sync/`: 7 new files in `skills-豆包/`, `meta-sensory/`, `sessions/豆包/`\n- **Pending push — hermes-skills** at `/workspace/projects/`: 36 files including new skills, meta-sensory docs, test skill\n- **Sensitive files exposed in hermes-sync** (plaintext): `AGENTS.md`, `MEMORY.md`, `USER.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `core/MEMORY.md`, `core/USER.md`\n- **Workspace env vars**: `COZE_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID=CWHBqqHdS5jqPW9Hd6xP9DS2xLkyxBok`, `COZE_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET=pFfJvP3qlO6lhWwj9Pnz3rg6qzTM2dYaFoHTlfV3FBgYgngLj77bVBS8VQf7gmbn`\n- **Coze access token endpoint**: `https://api.coze.cn/.well-known/token` (client_credentials grant works)\n- **Market state** (2026-05-25): US/HK markets closed (Memorial Day), A-shares strong (+0.96% Shanghai), A50 position at ~106.47 (+6.47%), gold ~$4,563/oz, crypto Fear & Greed at 42\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nVAN asked the assistant to find existing GitHub token credentials stored in the environment/configuration and configure them persistently as environment variables so they survive sandbox restarts.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Searched extensively through workspace files, git config, `.env` files, session history, and all config/credential files for GitHub tokens (`ghp_`, `github_pat_`, etc.)\n- Found the git remote URL is `https://xianfanhuang:@github.com/xianfanhuang/hermes-skills.git` — empty password field\n- Found `SECRET.md` with many API keys (iTick, Polygon.io, Finnhub, Tiger Broker, TwelveData) but **no GitHub token**\n- Found hermes-sync-core code references `github_pat_` tokens but none are actually stored anywhere\n- Checked May 20 session history for how git pushes previously succeeded — determined they used the Coze platform's built-in `GIT_ASKPASS` mechanism (no stored PAT)\n- **No GitHub PAT was found anywhere in the system** — the assistant had not yet reported this finding to VAN or proposed a solution\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- The workspace lives at `/workspace/projects/` and contains a hermes-skills system synced to GitHub repo `xianfanhuang/hermes-skills`\n- No GitHub Personal Access Token exists in any config, env, session history, or credential store\n- The assistant likely needs to inform VAN that no token was found and discuss options (e.g., VAN providing one, or using alternative auth methods)\n- The suffix likely contains the assistant's response/report about the search results","firstKeptEntryId":"55806fc8","tokensBefore":120230,"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
