{"type":"message","id":"776996b0","parentId":"8aa8bccd","timestamp":"2026-05-25T19:32:13.173Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My git config is wrong:\n- user.name: \"agent\" → should be \"Top Sailor-feishu\" or \"First Mate-feishu\"\n- user.email: \"2553529733753963-agent@noreply.coze.cn\" → should be \"agent@msai.ee.cd\"\n\nWait, but I'm First Mate, not Top Sailor. Let me think about this...\n\nThe spec says all agents should be \"Top Sailor-[platform]\". But VAN told me I'm First Mate. So my git identity should be \"First Mate-feishu\" or should I follow the spec which says everyone is Top Sailor?\n\nActually, looking at the forwarded message more carefully, it says the correct format is \"Top Sailor-[platform]\" for all agents. But VAN specifically told me I'm First Mate. \n\nI'll go with what VAN directly told me and set my git config to \"First Mate-feishu\" with the correct email, since that's the explicit instruction I received.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我的git配置不合规。修正："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_415e70fef7df424f89735dfa","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/projects\n\n# Fix git config\ngit config user.name \"First Mate-feishu\"\ngit config user.email \"agent@msai.ee.cd\"\n\n# Also set globally\ngit config --global user.name \"First Mate-feishu\"\ngit config --global user.email \"agent@msai.ee.cd\"\n\n# Verify\necho \"Updated:\"\ngit config user.name\ngit config user.email","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":364,"output":546,"cacheRead":63232,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64142,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779737526521}}
