{"type":"message","id":"619e476f","parentId":"69b204d1","timestamp":"2026-05-25T19:46:10.064Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the YAML error! Line 68 has a syntax issue. The Python code inside the YAML has a colon in the dictionary literal that's being interpreted as a YAML mapping. The issue is in the Python code block inside the `run` step. The `receive_id\": chat_id,` line has a colon after the closing quote which YAML interprets as a mapping.\n\nThis is a common issue when embedding Python code in YAML. The solution is to use a multiline string with `|` or `>`, or escape the colons.\n\nLet me look at the specific issue more carefully. The problem is that the Python dictionary `{\"receive_id\": chat_id, ...}` has colons that YAML is interpreting. The `run: |` block should handle this correctly, but there might be an indentation issue.\n\n\nI think the real issue is that the multiline block isn't properly indented or the `|` syntax isn't being recognized correctly, causing YAML to parse the Python code as its own syntax instead of treating it as a literal string.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到原因了！YAML语法错误：\n\n```yaml\n\"receive_id\": chat_id,\n```\n\n第68行的冒号被YAML解析器当成了mapping。需要修正workflow文件。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2fb42c6baade4eb7a0f11cee","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Get the full workflow content\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: token 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\" -H \"Accept: application/vnd.github.v3.raw\" \"https://api.github.com/repos/xianfanhuang/hermes-sync/contents/.github/workflows/team-notice.yml\" > /tmp/team-notice.yml\n\n# Show lines around the error\nsed -n '60,75p' /tmp/team-notice.yml","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":350,"output":615,"cacheRead":74112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":75077,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopRea